note The Files tab shows the indexed files as a tree with covered/total symbols per file and per directory. The reader reaches for it to browse by directory and see coverage per file when there is no symbol or tour name to search by (browsing files). Top-level directories start open and deeper ones closed; clicking a directory flips it. Clicking a file opens it in the Source view at its first line; so does clicking a file row in the Symbols tab. Files where no symbol is covered are dimmed, and a file or directory without symbols shows no count. The header gives the total over the whole index.

